-- title:
--   Membership in the prime-valued cutoff set
-- statement:
--   For every natural number $R$ and every prime $p$, membership in the finite prime-valued cutoff set is characterized by the numerical upper bound
--   $$
--   p\in\mathcal P_{\le R}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad p\le R.
--   $$
--   The prime hypothesis is encoded by taking $p$ from the type of natural primes; $R$ may be zero or one.
